*Troparion:*
Woe is me, how shall I escape the torments awaiting me, having lived evilly here! How shall I appear, wretched one, before the fearful Judge;
but do thou, O Mother of God and Sovereign Lady, be my helper then.

*Hypakoe, Tone 2:*
After the Passion the women went unto the Tomb to anoint Thy Body, O Christ God, and they saw Angels in the Tomb and were dismayed;
for they heard a voice from them: The Lord is risen, granting great mercy unto the world.[^388]
